  "details": "For context: When a personal mirror set to \"immersive mode\" and it is open in front of a menu in VR, the pointer raycast stops at the mirror instead of the menu which can interfere with interacting with buttons properly. This behaviour is not a big deal when using the Main Menu as the personal mirror keybind can be pressed again to close it.\n\n**The issue** is that this cannot be done when the chatbox is open. If the personal mirror is open and the chatbox is opened, the personal mirror keybind does not work. The player is forced to close the chatbox, turn off the mirror, then re-open the chatbox. This can sometimes cause frustrating moments as a chatbox user where I quickly begin typing only to realize I'm making typos because the raycasts are stopping at the mirror before the keys.\n\nThere could be an argument made that the raycast hitting the mirror should be disabled as a more broadly-applicable fix to this, which I would also be happy with. I just want to report the issue and present both solutions in case one is an easier fix than the other.\n\n# Steps to reproduce\n\n- Launch VRChat in VR mode\n\n- Set a controller button to \"Toggle Personal Mirror\" in SteamVR's Input binding settings for VRChat\n\n- Open the Main Menu\n\n- Notice that the Toggle Personal Mirror keybind works correctly\n\n- Open the Chatbox\n\n- Notice that the Toggle Personal Mirror keybind **does not** work correctly\n\n# Notes:\n\n- This issue has been occurring since Steam Input was implemented.",
